From d12e6401239e6e0a03aabf9761c3481c6e74739a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SriAkhilSJ <206201543+SriAkhilSJ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 03:55:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(preview): drop the connection resets under load, and stop
 fighting Windows

Two failures the user hit on the laptop, both reproduced here first.

Resets: a refused registration answered 403 without reading the request body, so
close() sent RST instead of FIN. Under 300 parallel refused registrations that
is 5 ConnectionResetError on the client, and on a keep-alive connection the
unread body desynchronised the next request into a 400. _drain_request_body()
now reads (and discards) up to _MAX_BODY before the 403 and before the
unrouted-POST 404. The second cause was the default listen backlog of 5:
HTTPServer drops the overflow, so 300 simultaneous connections reset ~4 of them
no matter what the handler does. _PreviewHTTPServer sets request_queue_size=128
(plus daemon_threads and allow_reuse_address). Proof: pre-fix hammer 5/300
resets, refused-POST-then-GET 400; post-fix 3 x 300 resets, 0.

Windows: os.replace() fails with WinError 5/32 when a reader (antivirus, the
IDE polling the endpoint file) holds the destination, so _publish() retries up
to 10 times with 10ms x (n+1) backoff, writes through a timestamped temp name,
and cleans it up in a finally. test_preview_contract.py used a bare path as an
ESM specifier (works on POSIX by accident, ERR_UNSUPPORTED_ESM_URL_SCHEME on
Windows) and decoded subprocess output with the host locale; it now builds a
file:// URL with pathToFileURL and asks for utf-8 with errors="replace".

Tests: 61 -> 66. The two new server tests fail on the old code (one
deterministically, over a keep-alive socket) and the two endpoint tests cover
the retry and the temp-file cleanup.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
